### Journal entry map modes (vanilla 1.15; docs/systems/mod_systems/journal_map_modes.md), third pass, 2026-11-05.
### A journal entry's map shows (the engine switches to it from code) while its page is open, and only then: the lens
### toolbar's lock doesn't keep it, and no other panel paints it (play-test checks 5 and 6). So a "show on the map"
### button is a button that opens the page. Every button here names its entry through a datacontext and passes
### JournalEntry.AccessSelf: inside a callback, GetPlayerJournalEntry fails at load both bare and ended with .AccessSelf
### ("requires non const promote"; gui_modding_guide.md gotcha #29).
###   - te_jmap_demog_map_button, in the Demographics tab's header (te_demog_window_body): one click picks life
###     expectancy and opens the Map Room (je_te_map_room, contextless, in no journal, there from the game's start);
###   - te_jmap_banking_map_button, in the Banking tab's header (te_banking_tab_body): opens je_banking_cycle, which
###     every country holds active from the engine's first check, before its cycle starts.
### Both clear the see-through flag first, so a page they open is whole.
### Both sit left of the header's "?" (te_help_button, 10 in from the right; this one 45 in), hidden for an observer.
###
### te_jmap_pick_row is the Map Room's picks: scripted GUIs, since the engine locks a contextless entry's own scripted
### buttons for a country not involved in it. It sits on the Map Room's page (te_map_room_widget.gui). The map takes a
### new pick at the next tick, and at once when the page reopens (check 4), so each pick has te_jmap_repainter (below,
### a scripted widget) close the page a tenth of a second after the click, for the scripted GUI's effect to land
### (a quarter second worked, sixth session), and open it again a fifth of a second later (a tenth worked; the fifth
### pass's twentieth for each sometimes left the page closed, 2026-11-07).
###
### Any journal page can be made see-through (the eye in its header, gui/journal_entry.gui), to look at its map. The
### flag outlives a pick's reopen, so a faded Map Room stays faded from map to map.

types te_map_widgets
{
	### The round map button: vanilla's States map mode icon on the small round button the "?" uses.
	type te_map_button = button_icon_round {
		blockoverride "size" {
			size = { 29 29 }
		}
		blockoverride "icon" {
			texture = "gfx/interface/icons/map_mode_icons/states.dds"
		}
	}

	### Demographics: pick life expectancy and open the Map Room, in one click. Opening the page repaints the map; whether
	### the pick has landed by then while paused is third-pass check 4 (if not, the delayed reopen the picks use).
	type te_jmap_demog_map_button = widget {
		size = { 29 29 }
		parentanchor = right|vcenter
		position = { -45 0 }
		visible = "[Not( GetMetaPlayer.IsObserver )]"

		te_map_button = {
			datacontext = "[GetPlayerJournalEntry('je_te_map_room')]"
			tooltip = "te_jmap_demog_button_tt"
			onclick = "[GetVariableSystem.Clear('te_je_see_through')]"
			onclick = "[GetScriptedGui('te_jmap_pick_life_expectancy_sgui').Execute( GuiScope.SetRoot( GetPlayer.MakeScope ).End )]"
			onclick = "[InformationPanelBar.OpenJournalEntryPanel(JournalEntry.AccessSelf)]"
		}
	}

	### Banking: every country holds the entry, so the button only opens it (vanilla's own pattern, states_panel.gui's
	### Meiji domain button: the entry as datacontext, then OpenJournalEntryPanel). No IsActive gate: the entry is active
	### for every country from the engine's first check (possible = yes), and the tab waits for that anyway; an inactive
	### page would open and paint too (check 7).
	type te_jmap_banking_map_button = widget {
		size = { 29 29 }
		parentanchor = right|vcenter
		position = { -45 0 }
		visible = "[Not( GetMetaPlayer.IsObserver )]"

		te_map_button = {
			datacontext = "[GetPlayerJournalEntry('je_banking_cycle')]"
			tooltip = "te_jmap_banking_button_tt"
			onclick = "[GetVariableSystem.Clear('te_je_see_through')]"
			onclick = "[InformationPanelBar.OpenJournalEntryPanel(JournalEntry.AccessSelf)]"
		}
	}

	### The systems' tabs: one click picks the system's map and opens the Map Room, as the Demographics button does.
	### The Map Room, not the system's own entry, though each entry draws the same map: the Map Room is there for every
	### country from the start, while several of these entries are held only by some countries, or not yet (the
	### nuclear program before its technology, covert warfare before its slots, a monument's owner, an empire with
	### colonies), and an entry nobody holds gives a button nothing to open. Each sits left of its header's "?". Each
	### notes the player as the maps' viewer before it picks: a pick already made is invalid, so its effect doesn't run.

	type te_jmap_gw_map_button = widget {
		size = { 29 29 }
		parentanchor = right|vcenter
		position = { -45 0 }
		visible = "[Not( GetMetaPlayer.IsObserver )]"

		### The Global Warming tab (te_gw_tab_body, also the Market panel's Climate tab).
		te_map_button = {
			datacontext = "[GetPlayerJournalEntry('je_te_map_room')]"
			tooltip = "te_jmap_gw_button_tt"
			onclick = "[GetVariableSystem.Clear('te_je_see_through')]"
			onclick = "[GetScriptedGui('te_jmap_note_viewer_sgui').Execute( GuiScope.SetRoot( GetPlayer.MakeScope ).End )]"
			onclick = "[GetScriptedGui('te_jmap_pick_emissions_sgui').Execute( GuiScope.SetRoot( GetPlayer.MakeScope ).End )]"
			onclick = "[InformationPanelBar.OpenJournalEntryPanel(JournalEntry.AccessSelf)]"
		}
	}

	type te_jmap_nuclear_map_button = widget {
		size = { 29 29 }
		parentanchor = right|vcenter
		position = { -45 0 }
		visible = "[Not( GetMetaPlayer.IsObserver )]"

		### The Nuclear Weapons tab (te_nuclear_tab_body).
